# School branding

`resolveSchoolBrand` is the only URL → brand lookup. Null, empty, and unknown URLs return `defaultSchoolBrand` (`alternateIconName: null`, asset `assets/icon/app_icon.png`).

Match order: host with `www.` stripped, then normalized full URL, then bare host. A new school uses the same id in `_brandsById`, `_hostToBrandId`, and `_fullUrlToBrandId`.

`alternateIconName` must match:

- Android alias `${applicationId}.MainActivity.{id}` in `android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml`. Tenant aliases stay `enabled="false"`; only `.MainActivity.default` starts enabled.
- The iOS `CFBundleAlternateIcons` key in both `CFBundleIcons` and `CFBundleIcons~ipad`.

In-app logo: `assets/icon/tenants/{id}.png` (`assets/icon/tenants/` is already a pubspec directory asset). OS icons are separate: `mipmap-*/ic_{id}.png` and `ios/Runner/{id}@2x.png`, `@3x.png`, `@2x~ipad.png`, `@3x~ipad.png`.

`android/app/src/debug/AndroidManifest.xml` adds MAIN/LAUNCHER on `MainActivity` and disables the default alias so `flutter run` can launch. Leave that debug merge in place.

When adding a tenant, follow `.cursor/skills/add-school-brand/SKILL.md`.
